{%- comment %}
Note to self:
This plugin picks an outfit sprite for the current weather
and shows a short hint about how the rest of the day will change.

Below I set up:
- sprite base URLs
- form field values (location, sarcasm level, future hints)
- shared time info (local time, day stamp)
- weather band + outfit slug
- future window and scenario
- text libraries for each scenario and sarcasm level
- final layout

Scenario logic v2:
Temp hints are now classified by DESTINATION zone, not just direction.
- zone(t): cold if t <= 7, hot if t > 27, else mid
- warmer -> variant by zone(max_temp_future): warmer_cold / warmer / warmer_hot
- colder -> variant by zone(min_temp_future): colder_hot / colder_mid / colder
- temp_state additionally gated on a band change (delta alone is not enough)
- detection is sequence aware: when both a significant warm up and a
  significant cool down exist in the window, the EARLIER one wins
- warm up followed by significant cool down maps to the arc scenario
  (shed layers midday, want them back in the evening)
- combo scenarios fall back to plain precip scenario when the temp flavor
  contradicts the destination zone (wetter_warmer with cold dest -> wetter, etc.)
- forecast horizon is now fixed (end of active day) instead of time boxed,
  because sequence aware detection removes the evening cool off bias
{%- endcomment %}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Assign sprite URLs.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign sprite_base_url  = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nikokoren/what-to-wear/refs/heads/main/' -%}
{%- assign error_sprite_url = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nikokoren/what-to-wear/refs/heads/main/404.png' -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Read custom field values from the TRMNL settings.
Using default filter to handle nil values efficiently.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign location_label_raw = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.location_label | default: '' -%}
{%- assign latitude_str = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.latitude | default: '' -%}
{%- assign longitude_str = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.longitude | default: '' -%}
{%- assign show_future_suggestions_raw = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.show_future_suggestions | default: 'on' -%}
{%- assign language_raw = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.language | default: 'es' -%}
{%- assign sarcasm_level_raw = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.sarcasm_level | default: '0' -%}
{%- assign show_bottom_bar = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.show_bottom_bar | default: 'on' -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Normalise show_future_suggestions to "on" or "off"
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign show_future_suggestions = 'on' -%}
{%- assign sfs_check = show_future_suggestions_raw | downcase | strip -%}
{%- if sfs_check == 'no' or sfs_check == 'false' or sfs_check == '0' -%}
  {%- assign show_future_suggestions = 'off' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Normalise language to "en", "de", or "es".
Fallback to Peruvian Spanish.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign lang = language_raw | downcase | strip -%}
{%- if lang != 'de' and lang != 'en' and lang != 'es' -%}
  {%- assign lang = 'es' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Normalise sarcasm_level to one of "0", "10", "11".
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign sarcasm_level = '0' -%}
{%- assign sarc_check = sarcasm_level_raw | strip -%}
{%- if sarc_check == '10' or sarc_check == '11' -%}
  {%- assign sarcasm_level = sarc_check -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
If the user did not give a label, I show nothing in the title bar.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign location_label = location_label_raw -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Get current weather and hourly objects from the Open Meteo recipe.
If either is missing, I treat it as an error and show an error message.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign cw = current -%}
{%- assign h = hourly -%}
{%- assign is_error = false -%}
{%- assign error_message = '' -%}

{%- if cw == nil -%}
  {%- assign is_error = true -%}
  {%- if lang == 'de' -%}
    {%- assign error_message = 'Wetterdaten konnten nicht abgerufen werden. Bitte versuche es spÃ¤ter erneut.' -%}
  {%- elsif lang == 'es' -%}
    {%- assign error_message = 'No se pudieron cargar los datos del clima. Intenta de nuevo más tarde.' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign error_message = 'Unable to retrieve weather data. Please try again later.' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- elsif h == nil -%}
  {%- assign is_error = true -%}
  {%- if lang == 'de' -%}
    {%- assign error_message = 'Wettervorhersage konnte nicht geladen werden. Bitte versuche es spÃ¤ter erneut.' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign error_message = 'Unable to load forecast data. Please try again later.' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if is_error and lang == 'es' -%}
  {%- assign error_message = 'No se pudieron cargar los datos del clima. Intenta de nuevo más tarde.' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Shared time info.
Prefer API time, fallback to device time if unavailable.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign local_hour = 12 -%}
{%- assign today_md = '01-01' -%}

{%- if current.time -%}
  {%- assign local_hour = current.time | slice: 11, 2 | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign today_md = current.time | slice: 5, 5 -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign epoch_utc = trmnl.system.timestamp_utc | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign utc_offset = trmnl.user.utc_offset | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign local_secs = epoch_utc | plus: utc_offset -%}
  {%- assign local_hour = local_secs | divided_by: 3600 | modulo: 24 -%}
  {%- assign today_md = local_secs | date: '%m-%d' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Calculate local_days for hint rotation (uses UTC timestamp for consistency)
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign epoch_utc = trmnl.system.timestamp_utc | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign local_days = epoch_utc | divided_by: 86400 -%}

{%- assign dev_width = trmnl.device.width | plus: 0 -%}

{%- assign is_og = false -%}

{%- if dev_width <= 800 -%}
  {%- assign is_og = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Set up defaults so Liquid never chokes on nil.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign temp_c = 0 -%}
{%- assign wmo = 0 -%}
{%- assign is_now_precip = 0 -%}
{%- assign band = 'mild' -%}
{%- assign weather_slug = '' -%}

{%- assign max_temp_future = 0 -%}
{%- assign min_temp_future = 0 -%}
{%- assign max_rain_future = 0 -%}
{%- assign has_future_window = false -%}
{%- assign max_temp_idx = 0 -%}
{%- assign min_temp_idx = 0 -%}

{%- assign today_tip = '' -%}
{%- assign scenario = '' -%}
{%- assign precip_state = 'none' -%}
{%- assign temp_state = 'flat' -%}
{%- assign dest_temp = 0 -%}
{%- assign dest_zone = 'mid' -%}

{%- if is_error == false -%}

  {%- comment %}
  Note to self:
  Read current temperature and WMO code,
  then decide if it is precipitating right now.
  Consolidated into single conditional.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign temp_c = cw.apparent_temperature | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign wmo = cw.weather_code | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}

  {%- if wmo >= 51 and wmo <= 67 or wmo >= 71 and wmo <= 77 or wmo >= 80 and wmo <= 82 or wmo >= 95 -%}
    {%- assign is_now_precip = 1 -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment %}
  Note to self:
  Map current temperature to a band.
  I use this band name for the outfit sprite.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- if temp_c <= 0 -%}
    {%- assign band = 'freezing' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_c <= 7 -%}
    {%- assign band = 'cold' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_c <= 14 -%}
    {%- assign band = 'cool' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_c <= 20 -%}
    {%- assign band = 'mild' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_c <= 27 -%}
    {%- assign band = 'warm' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_c <= 32 -%}
    {%- assign band = 'hot' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign band = 'very_hot' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment %}
  Note to self:
  Turn band plus current precipitation into a base outfit slug.
  Using string concatenation instead of nested if/elsif.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign precip_suffix = 'dry' -%}
  {%- if is_now_precip == 1 -%}
    {%- if band == 'freezing' -%}
      {%- assign precip_suffix = 'snow' -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign precip_suffix = 'rain' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- assign weather_slug = band | append: '_' | append: precip_suffix -%}

  {%- comment %}
  Note to self:
  Fixed forecast horizon. Detection is now sequence aware
  (the first significant change wins), so I no longer need
  the old time of day boxes to suppress the evening cool off bias.
  - Look until the end of the active day (day_end_hour)
  - Always keep at least a 3 hour window in the evening
  - Never look past 23:00
  {%- endcomment %}

  {%- assign day_end_hour = 21 -%}
  {%- assign cutoff_hour = day_end_hour -%}
  {%- assign min_cutoff = local_hour | plus: 3 -%}
  {%- if min_cutoff > cutoff_hour -%}
    {%- assign cutoff_hour = min_cutoff -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if cutoff_hour > 23 -%}
    {%- assign cutoff_hour = 23 -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if cutoff_hour > local_hour -%}
    {%- assign temps = h.apparent_temperature -%}
    {%- assign probs = h.precipitation_probability -%}
    {%- assign h_count = temps | size | default: 0 -%}

    {%- if temps != nil and probs != nil and h_count > 0 -%}
      {%- assign start_index = local_hour | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- assign end_index = cutoff_hour -%}
      {%- assign last_index = h_count | minus: 1 -%}

      {%- if start_index <= end_index and start_index <= last_index -%}
        {%- if end_index > last_index -%}
          {%- assign end_index = last_index -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- assign has_future_window = true -%}
        {%- assign max_temp_future = temp_c -%}
        {%- assign min_temp_future = temp_c -%}
        {%- assign max_temp_idx = start_index -%}
        {%- assign min_temp_idx = start_index -%}
        {%- assign max_rain_future = 0 -%}

        {%- for t in temps -%}
          {%- assign i = forloop.index0 -%}
          {%- if i >= start_index and i <= end_index -%}
            {%- assign tv = t | plus: 0 -%}
            {%- if tv > max_temp_future -%}
              {%- assign max_temp_future = tv -%}
              {%- assign max_temp_idx = i -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if tv < min_temp_future -%}
              {%- assign min_temp_future = tv -%}
              {%- assign min_temp_idx = i -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- for p in probs -%}
          {%- assign i = forloop.index0 -%}
          {%- if i >= start_index and i <= end_index -%}
            {%- assign pv = p | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
            {%- if pv > max_rain_future -%}
              {%- assign max_rain_future = pv -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign has_future_window = false -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign has_future_window = false -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    
  {%- elsif cutoff_hour == local_hour and local_hour == 23 -%}
    {%- comment %} Special case: At exactly 23:00, just say "perfect" {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign has_future_window = false -%}
    {%- assign scenario = 'perfect' -%}
    
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign has_future_window = false -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if has_future_window -%}

    {%- comment %}
    Note to self:
    Sequence aware temperature detection.
    A direction only counts as significant if the delta is >= 3
    AND the destination temperature crosses into a different band
    (a 3 degree wiggle inside the same band does not deserve a hint).
    If BOTH directions are significant, the one that happens FIRST wins.
    Warm up first plus cool down later is the classic arc day and
    gets its own scenario. Cool down first plus warm up later keeps
    it simple: the first change (colder) is the primary hint.
    dest_temp is the temperature the primary hint is heading towards.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign delta_up = max_temp_future | minus: temp_c -%}
    {%- assign delta_down = temp_c | minus: min_temp_future -%}

    {%- assign warm_significant = false -%}
    {%- if delta_up >= 3 -%}
      {%- assign up_band = 'mild' -%}
      {%- if max_temp_future <= 0 -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'freezing' -%}
      {%- elsif max_temp_future <= 7 -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'cold' -%}
      {%- elsif max_temp_future <= 14 -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'cool' -%}
      {%- elsif max_temp_future <= 20 -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'mild' -%}
      {%- elsif max_temp_future <= 27 -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'warm' -%}
      {%- elsif max_temp_future <= 32 -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'hot' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign up_band = 'very_hot' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if up_band != band -%}
        {%- assign warm_significant = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- assign cold_significant = false -%}
    {%- if delta_down >= 3 -%}
      {%- assign down_band = 'mild' -%}
      {%- if min_temp_future <= 0 -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'freezing' -%}
      {%- elsif min_temp_future <= 7 -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'cold' -%}
      {%- elsif min_temp_future <= 14 -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'cool' -%}
      {%- elsif min_temp_future <= 20 -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'mild' -%}
      {%- elsif min_temp_future <= 27 -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'warm' -%}
      {%- elsif min_temp_future <= 32 -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'hot' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign down_band = 'very_hot' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if down_band != band -%}
        {%- assign cold_significant = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- assign temp_state = 'flat' -%}
    {%- assign dest_temp = temp_c -%}
    {%- if warm_significant and cold_significant -%}
      {%- if max_temp_idx <= min_temp_idx -%}
        {%- assign temp_state = 'arc' -%}
        {%- assign dest_temp = max_temp_future -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign temp_state = 'colder' -%}
        {%- assign dest_temp = min_temp_future -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- elsif warm_significant -%}
      {%- assign temp_state = 'warmer' -%}
      {%- assign dest_temp = max_temp_future -%}
    {%- elsif cold_significant -%}
      {%- assign temp_state = 'colder' -%}
      {%- assign dest_temp = min_temp_future -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment %}
    Note to self:
    Destination zone drives which text flavor fits:
    - cold: dest <= 7 (still coat weather no matter what)
    - hot: dest > 27 (no layers left to add or remove)
    - mid: everything in between (classic layer advice applies)
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign dest_zone = 'mid' -%}
    {%- if dest_temp <= 7 -%}
      {%- assign dest_zone = 'cold' -%}
    {%- elsif dest_temp > 27 -%}
      {%- assign dest_zone = 'hot' -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment %}
    Note to self:
    Determine precip_state for hints:
    - wetter: dry now, rain chance later
    - drier: wet now, dries out later
    - none: everything else, including stays_wet
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign precip_state = 'none' -%}
    {%- assign rain_threshold = 20 -%}

    {%- if is_now_precip == 0 -%}
      {%- if max_rain_future >= rain_threshold -%}
        {%- assign precip_state = 'wetter' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- if max_rain_future < rain_threshold -%}
        {%- assign precip_state = 'drier' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment %}
    Note to self:
    Map precip_state, temp_state and dest_zone to scenario.
    Pure temp scenarios:
    - arc: warm up first, significant cool down after (layers off, then back on)
    - warmer_cold: milder but still cold, keep the coat
    - warmer: the classic shed a layer case (mid destination)
    - warmer_hot: real heat, shade and hydration
    - colder: the classic add real warmth case (cold destination)
    - colder_mid: mild cooldown, one light layer
    - colder_hot: relief from heat, no layer needed
    Combos treat arc as its first leg (warmer) and fall back to the
    plain precip scenario when the temp flavor contradicts the
    destination zone.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign scenario = 'perfect' -%}

    {%- if precip_state == 'none' -%}
      {%- if temp_state == 'arc' -%}
        {%- assign scenario = 'arc' -%}
      {%- elsif temp_state == 'warmer' -%}
        {%- if dest_zone == 'cold' -%}
          {%- assign scenario = 'warmer_cold' -%}
        {%- elsif dest_zone == 'hot' -%}
          {%- assign scenario = 'warmer_hot' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign scenario = 'warmer' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- elsif temp_state == 'colder' -%}
        {%- if dest_zone == 'hot' -%}
          {%- assign scenario = 'colder_hot' -%}
        {%- elsif dest_zone == 'cold' -%}
          {%- assign scenario = 'colder' -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign scenario = 'colder_mid' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign scenario = precip_state -%}
      {%- assign combo_temp = temp_state -%}
      {%- if combo_temp == 'arc' -%}
        {%- assign combo_temp = 'warmer' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if combo_temp == 'warmer' -%}
        {%- if dest_zone != 'cold' -%}
          {%- assign scenario = scenario | append: '_warmer' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- elsif combo_temp == 'colder' -%}
        {%- if dest_zone == 'cold' -%}
          {%- assign scenario = scenario | append: '_colder' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment %}
    Note to self:
    No usable future window, but no hard error:
    treat as perfect outfit all day.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign scenario = 'perfect' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

{%- endif -%}

{%- comment %}
Note to self:
Text libraries for each scenario and sarcasm level.
I store variants in a single string and split into arrays.
Delimiter "||" must not appear in any text.
{%- endcomment %}

{%- comment %} Scenario: Perfect {% endcomment %}
{%- assign hints_perfect_0_en = "Conditions remain stable. You are set for the rest of the day.||The forecast holds steady. No outfit changes needed later.||Conditions stay the same. You can trust this outfit.||Stable weather ahead. Keep your layers as they are.||No surprises incoming. This outfit keeps working.||The weather will hold. Your outfit works the rest of the day.||Forecast stays flat. You can keep wearing this outfit.||Nothing shifts later. No need to adjust a single layer.||Same conditions for the rest of the day. This outfit remains the right choice.||No changes on the horizon. Stay as you are." | split: "||" -%}
{%- assign hints_perfect_10_en = "The weather is on cruise control. No need to overthink your outfit options.||Boring forecast ahead. Your clothing choice can stay drama-free.||Mother Nature is feeling lazy. Your current look works for the rest of the day.||Nothing changes later. Your outfit will be bored, but still effective.||Shockingly, this outfit actually works the rest of the day.||Forecast update: still nothing. Your outfit can keep pretending this is exciting.||Weather remains committed to doing the bare minimum. So can your wardrobe.||The sky phones it in like a Monday morning work call. Keep the outfit, save the effort.||The forecast has reached a creative standstill. Your outfit will remain correct.||Nothing new develops later. Feel free to stop second-guessing your layers.||Stability all day. Your outfit does not need a backup plan.||This day is on repeat like a broken playlist. Wear the same thing, save the effort.||Weather.exe has stopped responding. Keep wearing what you have.||The atmosphere phoned it in. So can you." | split: "||" -%}
{%- assign hints_perfect_11_en = "Relentless monotony ahead. You are stuck in this outfit for the rest of the day.||The atmosphere has flatlined. Accept your sartorial destiny and stop touching your layers.||The sky refuses to be interesting. Keep wearing what you have, it will not get better.||The weather refuses to change. Keep what you are wearing, it stays the least bad option.||A void of weather events. Do nothing, wear the same outfit, survive the boredom.||Existence is repetitive, and so is this forecast. Stay put in your current layers.||Nothing moves later. Especially not your outfit, so keep it exactly as is.||Change has been formally denied. Your outfit is sentenced until evening, do not try to appeal.||Nothing will happen later. Not to the weather. Not to your clothes.||Stability becomes tyranny. Keep the same layers and pretend this is freedom.||The sky denies change. Keep your outfit unchanged, because change is not on the menu.||The forecast enters a loop. You and this outfit are trapped together until evening.||The forecast refuses to evolve. You and this outfit are paired until evening.||The forecast is Groundhog Day, but without the charm. Keep the outfit. Do not negotiate with your layers.||Nothing changes. You and this outfit are in a committed relationship until evening.||Weather has become a philosophical concept: unchanging, meaningless, inescapable." | split: "||" -%}

{%- assign hints_perfect_0_de = "Die Lage bleibt stabil. Dein Outfit passt für den gesamten Tag.||Keine Wetteränderung in Sicht. Du kannst so angezogen bleiben.||Der Wetterbericht bleibt ruhig. An deiner Kleidung muss nichts mehr geändert werden.||Konstantes Wetter voraus. Deine Kleidung passt perfekt für den restlichen Tag.||Die Wetterlage bleibt unverändert. Dein aktuelles Outfit funktioniert den ganzen Tag.||Ruhige Aussichten für den weiteren Wetterverlauf. Kleidungstechnisch bist du gut aufgestellt.||Das Wetter hält Kurs. Keine weiteren Anpassungen an deiner Kleidung nötig.||Das Wetter bleibt bis zum Abend stabil. Du kannst bei diesem Outfit bleiben." | split: "||" -%}
{%- assign hints_perfect_10_de = "Petrus macht heute Dienst nach Vorschrift. Das Outfit passt für den restlichen Tag.||Das Wetter läuft auf Autopilot. Du musst dir keine weiteren Gedanken über dein Outfit machen.||Das Wetter macht keine Experimente. Du kannst so angezogen bleiben.||Kein Wetterdrama in Sicht. Spar dir die Mühe, dich umzuziehen.||Heute passiert wettertechnisch exakt gar nichts. Das Outfit passt für den restlichen Tag.||Prognose: Stillstand. Dein Outfit kann bleiben wie es ist.||Mutter Natur ist heute faul. Dein aktueller Look passt für den Rest des Tages.||Überraschenderweise funktioniert dieses Outfit tatsÃ¤chlich für den Rest des Tages.||Das Wetter ist so motiviert wie Bernd das Brot. Dein Outfit passt für den Rest des Tages." | split: "||" -%}
